-- title:
--   Radix indices distinguish residue-pair columns
-- statement:
--   For $h\in\mathbb N$, let $p=p_h$ be the chosen local prime. Encode an index $r<p^2$ by its quotient and remainder as a pair in $(\mathbb Z/p\mathbb Z)^2$:
--
--   $$\tau_h(r)=\left(\left\lfloor\frac r p\right\rfloor\bmod p,\ r\bmod p\right).$$
--
--   This map is injective on its column-index range:
--
--   $$x,y<p^2\ \land\ \tau_h(x)=\tau_h(y)\quad\Longrightarrow\quad x=y.$$
--
--   The result verifies that row-major matrix columns represent distinct residue-pair targets in the local-cover problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverSchedule.lean#L31-L46

